      "id": 2,
      "type": "manual",
      "desc": "(b) must say that x = 3 is a hole and x = -2 is a vertical asymptote, with the reason drawn from the factored form: the factor (x-3) appears on top and on the bottom and cancels, so that value is a single missing point, while (x+2) survives the cancelling and drives the function to infinity. Naming the two correctly without the cancelling reason earns partial credit only.",
      "slot": "(b) which is a hole, which is an asymptote, and why",
      "skill": "classify-discontinuity",
